# This is not an allowlist of paths. Each line names one finding in one commit that has already
# happened, so nothing a future commit adds can hide behind it — which is the only kind of gitleaks
# exception worth having. A path-shaped or rule-shaped entry would keep its exemption long after the
# line that earned it was gone, and the next real leak would land inside it quietly.
